{"name":"Dancer","hex":"#dc9399","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dancer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The second reindeer of Santa Claus.","A surname originating as an occupation for a dancer or acrobat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dancer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/GDC_onlywayaround.jpg/500px-GDC_onlywayaround.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/GDC_onlywayaround.jpg/500px-GDC_onlywayaround.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Members of an American jazz dance company perform a formal group routine in a concert dance setting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGDC_onlywayaround.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg/500px-Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg/1280px-Dancing_painting_at_Bhimbetka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","s